g  we really need to focus on other things  and actually you know you can go  down wormholes on this and it's you've  got to be a bit careful when you look at  these numbers because for instance okay  there was a chart recently doing the  rounds about how it looked terrifying  for the uk because our cases are going  up so fast and everyone else  in europe is going down this this is  more or less what the chart was showing  you so that red line is the uk let me  highlight it the red line  uh is the uk and those other lines are  uh germany and france  uh italy and the us as well and you can  see indeed they are going down the uk is  going up but  bear in mind we are testing a lot more  than most other countries uh around the  world  and that means that broadly speaking any  increase in growth is going to look  pretty sharp uh when it comes to the uk  so compare other charts i'm going to  bring a different chart on compare  something like hospital emissions  and while the uk certainly is rising it  doesn't look like we're kind of going  out up into the stratosphere like we  might have like it might have looked in  the other chart in fact we're  going up but relatively gently at the  moment you saw that previous chart i  showed you this is just comparing it  with countries around the eu same thing  with death in fact with deaths we're  well below  most other countries that are kind of  focused on here  it's worth bearing all of this in mind  because the hope is that we have  potentially broken  that chain and what's really happening  right now  uh is this thing this is just showing  you how much of the delta variant that  indian variant there is  in various countries around the eu and  what you can see from this  is that the uk had that increase about a  month or so  before everyone else but now you're  starting to see other countries starting  to get more  of the delta variants sweden spain  germany and the rest are starting to  pick up  so it's more the case that the 